<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Yao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 329</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Yao was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> general and the last emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-zhao">Han Zhao</a>. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shi-le">Shi Le</a> he captured the Jin capitals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> in 311 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> in 316. After a coup in 318 he took the throne, renaming the state Zhao, but his rival Shi Le founded Later Zhao, captured him in battle at Luoyang in 328 and had him killed.</p></div>
